<!-- FAQ -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions about Suspended Ceilings</h2>
<div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What is a suspended ceiling?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">A suspended ceiling is a secondary ceiling hung below the main structural ceiling. It creates a clean visual plane, hides services like ductwork and cabling, and allows easy access for maintenance.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">How long does suspended ceiling installation take?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">A typical office suspended ceiling takes 2-3 days. Larger commercial spaces may take 4-7 days depending on the area and any integrated services like lighting or air vents.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Can suspended ceilings improve acoustics?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. Acoustic ceiling tiles absorb sound and reduce noise levels in open-plan offices, meeting rooms, and call centres. We install mineral fibre and perforated metal tiles with NRC ratings up to 0.85 for optimal sound control.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Are suspended ceilings fire-rated?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. We install fire-rated ceiling systems that meet Part B building regulations. Fire-rated tiles and grid systems provide protection and slow the spread of fire through ceiling voids.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Can you integrate lighting into suspended ceilings?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. We can integrate LED panels, recessed downlights, emergency lighting, and air conditioning vents into suspended ceiling systems for a seamless, professional finish.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What types of ceiling tiles do you install?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">We install mineral fibre tiles, metal tiles (perforated and plain), plasterboard suspended ceilings, fire-rated tiles, and moisture-resistant tiles for kitchens and bathrooms.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What areas do you cover for suspended ceilings?</h3>
